90.67% of listed central enterprises already disclose ESG reports, reflecting rapid adoption.', 'Issued by the State-Owned Assets Supervision and Administration Commission (SASAC) on June 4, 2024, these guidelines provide a comprehensive framework for China’s central enterprises (央企) to integrate Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) principles into their corporate responsibility efforts. The guidelines emphasize high-standard social responsibility, economic leadership, and alignment with China’s sustainable development goals.

