The document also aligns with international frameworks, such as the EU Taxonomy for Sustainable Activities, facilitating cross-border green finance initiatives. By promoting transparency and consistency, it strengthens investor confidence and accelerates the growth of China’s green bond market.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2021-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_51', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'china']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('87ed066b-7d4e-555b-99c6-2421825f8f11', 'China Energy Law (Draft for Comment)', 'Energy Law of the People''s Republic of China (Draft for Comment)', 'The "Energy Law of the People''s Republic of China (Draft for Comment)" is a comprehensive framework designed to regulate energy development, utilization, supervision, and management across the nation. The draft aims to ensure energy security, optimize energy structure, and align energy practices with principles of ecological sustainability and innovation. Key provisions include promoting renewable energy, enhancing energy efficiency, and advancing clean energy technologies. The law emphasizes a market-driven energy system while maintaining government oversight for strategic planning and security. It also underscores international cooperation in energy development and technology exchange. Specific mechanisms for energy conservation, rural energy development, and the establishment of emergency reserves are detailed. Provisions for information disclosure and public participation are incorporated to ensure transparency and stakeholder engagement.', 'The "Energy Law of the People''s Republic of China (Draft for Comment)" is a comprehensive framework designed to regulate energy development, utilization, supervision, and management across the nation. The draft aims to ensure energy security, optimize energy structure, and align energy practices with principles of ecological sustainability and innovation. Key provisions include promoting renewable energy, enhancing energy efficiency, and advancing clean energy technologies. The law emphasizes a market-driven energy system while maintaining government oversight for strategic planning and security. It also underscores international cooperation in energy development and technology exchange. Specific mechanisms for energy conservation, rural energy development, and the establishment of emergency reserves are detailed. Provisions for information disclosure and public participation are incorporated to ensure transparency and stakeholder engagement.', 'The "Energy Law of the People''s Republic of China (Draft for Comment)" is a comprehensive framework designed to regulate energy development, utilization, supervision, and management across the nation. The draft aims to ensure energy security, optimize energy structure, and align energy practices with principles of ecological sustainability and innovation. Key provisions include promoting renewable energy, enhancing energy efficiency, and advancing clean energy technologies. The law emphasizes a market-driven energy system while maintaining government oversight for strategic planning and security. It also underscores international cooperation in energy development and technology exchange. Specific mechanisms for energy conservation, rural energy development, and the establishment of emergency reserves are detailed. Provisions for information disclosure and public participation are incorporated to ensure transparency and stakeholder engagement.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2020-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_23', ARRAY['regulations', 'sdg7', 'sdg17', 'china', 'mandatory', 'sdg6', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'sdg9']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('e75dd5b2-4a69-5284-8497-7d90d1d4d64f', 'China Green Trust Guidelines', 'Green Trust Guidelines', 'The "Green Trust Guidelines (2019)" outline principles and frameworks for promoting green finance in China through the activities of trust companies. Formulated by the China Trustee Association under the guidance of regulatory authorities, the guidelines aim to integrate green development strategies into trust practices. The policy focuses on investments in environmentally beneficial projects such as renewable energy, pollution control, and resource conservation. Trust companies are encouraged to innovate financial services like green equity, bonds, and asset securitization while prioritizing environmental and social risk management.

The guidelines establish obligations for trust companies to strengthen their organizational structures, adopt standards for environmental performance assessments, and disclose relevant information. By aligning with national and international green finance standards, the guidelines seek to foster sustainability in the trust industry and support ecological progress and resource-efficient economic development.', 'The "Green Trust Guidelines (2019)" outline principles and frameworks for promoting green finance in China through the activities of trust companies. Formulated by the China Trustee Association under the guidance of regulatory authorities, the guidelines aim to integrate green development strategies into trust practices. The policy focuses on investments in environmentally beneficial projects such as renewable energy, pollution control, and resource conservation. Trust companies are encouraged to innovate financial services like green equity, bonds, and asset securitization while prioritizing environmental and social risk management.

The guidelines establish obligations for trust companies to strengthen their organizational structures, adopt standards for environmental performance assessments, and disclose relevant information. By aligning with national and international green finance standards, the guidelines seek to foster sustainability in the trust industry and support ecological progress and resource-efficient economic development.', 'The "Green Trust Guidelines (2019)" outline principles and frameworks for promoting green finance in China through the activities of trust companies. Formulated by the China Trustee Association under the guidance of regulatory authorities, the guidelines aim to integrate green development strategies into trust practices. The policy focuses on investments in environmentally beneficial projects such as renewable energy, pollution control, and resource conservation. Trust companies are encouraged to innovate financial services like green equity, bonds, and asset securitization while prioritizing environmental and social risk management.

The guidelines establish obligations for trust companies to strengthen their organizational structures, adopt standards for environmental performance assessments, and disclose relevant information. By aligning with national and international green finance standards, the guidelines seek to foster sustainability in the trust industry and support ecological progress and resource-efficient economic development.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2020-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_48', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'sdg13', 'sdg7', 'china', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'sdg9', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('e382d1e5-345e-55fe-8b82-be56fd4137c6', 'China Promoting Investment and Financing to Address Climate Change', 'Guidance on Promoting Investment and Financing to Address Climate Change', 'The 2020 Guidance on Promoting Climate Change Financing and Investment outlines China’s strategic framework for integrating climate considerations into financial systems to support the country’s low-carbon transition. The document emphasizes the role of financial institutions and capital markets in mobilizing resources for climate mitigation and adaptation projects. It aligns with China''s commitment to achieving peak carbon emissions by 2030 and carbon neutrality by 2060.

Key provisions include incentivizing green financing through policy measures such as subsidies, tax incentives, and preferential lending rates. The guidance also promotes the development of green bonds, climate risk assessments, and climate-focused financial products. Financial institutions are encouraged to integrate climate risks into their governance structures, risk management frameworks, and disclosure practices.

The document highlights the need for international cooperation, aligning China’s climate financing frameworks with global standards. By fostering partnerships and improving disclosure practices, the guidance aims to attract foreign investments while enhancing transparency and accountability.', 'The 2020 Guidance on Promoting Climate Change Financing and Investment outlines China’s strategic framework for integrating climate considerations into financial systems to support the country’s low-carbon transition. The document emphasizes the role of financial institutions and capital markets in mobilizing resources for climate mitigation and adaptation projects. It aligns with China''s commitment to achieving peak carbon emissions by 2030 and carbon neutrality by 2060.

Key provisions include incentivizing green financing through policy measures such as subsidies, tax incentives, and preferential lending rates. The guidance also promotes the development of green bonds, climate risk assessments, and climate-focused financial products. Financial institutions are encouraged to integrate climate risks into their governance structures, risk management frameworks, and disclosure practices.

The document highlights the need for international cooperation, aligning China’s climate financing frameworks with global standards. By fostering partnerships and improving disclosure practices, the guidance aims to attract foreign investments while enhancing transparency and accountability.', 'The 2020 Guidance on Promoting Climate Change Financing and Investment outlines China’s strategic framework for integrating climate considerations into financial systems to support the country’s low-carbon transition. The document emphasizes the role of financial institutions and capital markets in mobilizing resources for climate mitigation and adaptation projects. It aligns with China''s commitment to achieving peak carbon emissions by 2030 and carbon neutrality by 2060.

Key provisions include incentivizing green financing through policy measures such as subsidies, tax incentives, and preferential lending rates. The guidance also promotes the development of green bonds, climate risk assessments, and climate-focused financial products. Financial institutions are encouraged to integrate climate risks into their governance structures, risk management frameworks, and disclosure practices.

The document highlights the need for international cooperation, aligning China’s climate financing frameworks with global standards. By fostering partnerships and improving disclosure practices, the guidance aims to attract foreign investments while enhancing transparency and accountability.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2020-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_50', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'sdg13', 'sdg7', 'sdg17', 'china', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'sdg9']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('afacd3eb-01b6-5ca8-8476-cc92b2b5d8db', 'China Notice on Issuing the Rules for the Listing', 'Notice on Issuing the Rules for the Listing of Stocks on the Science and Technology Innovation Board of the Shanghai Stock Exchange', 'The revised Rules for Listing Stocks on the SSE STAR Market (2020) establish updated criteria and procedures for companies seeking to list on the Shanghai Stock Exchange’s STAR Market, a platform designed for high-tech and innovative enterprises. The revisions aim to enhance market transparency, protect investors, and promote the sustainable growth of listed companies. Key changes focus on delisting standards, optimized procedures, and stricter requirements for financial disclosures and corporate governance.

The rules emphasize compliance with sustainability and innovation goals, encouraging companies to adopt robust governance practices and transparent reporting frameworks. Specific provisions include the introduction of stricter financial thresholds for continued listing, measures to prevent fraudulent disclosures, and enhanced penalties for violations. Companies must also disclose environmental, social, and governance (ESG) information, aligning with China’s broader goals for sustainable development.

The revised rules align the SSE STAR Market with international best practices, attracting global investors and fostering cross-border capital flows.', 'The revised Rules for Listing Stocks on the SSE STAR Market (2020) establish updated criteria and procedures for companies seeking to list on the Shanghai Stock Exchange’s STAR Market, a platform designed for high-tech and innovative enterprises. The revisions aim to enhance market transparency, protect investors, and promote the sustainable growth of listed companies. Key changes focus on delisting standards, optimized procedures, and stricter requirements for financial disclosures and corporate governance.

The rules emphasize compliance with sustainability and innovation goals, encouraging companies to adopt robust governance practices and transparent reporting frameworks. Specific provisions include the introduction of stricter financial thresholds for continued listing, measures to prevent fraudulent disclosures, and enhanced penalties for violations. Companies must also disclose environmental, social, and governance (ESG) information, aligning with China’s broader goals for sustainable development.

The revised rules align the SSE STAR Market with international best practices, attracting global investors and fostering cross-border capital flows.', 'The revised Rules for Listing Stocks on the SSE STAR Market (2020) establish updated criteria and procedures for companies seeking to list on the Shanghai Stock Exchange’s STAR Market, a platform designed for high-tech and innovative enterprises. The revisions aim to enhance market transparency, protect investors, and promote the sustainable growth of listed companies. Key changes focus on delisting standards, optimized procedures, and stricter requirements for financial disclosures and corporate governance.

The rules emphasize compliance with sustainability and innovation goals, encouraging companies to adopt robust governance practices and transparent reporting frameworks. Specific provisions include the introduction of stricter financial thresholds for continued listing, measures to prevent fraudulent disclosures, and enhanced penalties for violations. Companies must also disclose environmental, social, and governance (ESG) information, aligning with China’s broader goals for sustainable development.

The revised rules align the SSE STAR Market with international best practices, attracting global investors and fostering cross-border capital flows.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2020-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_67', ARRAY['regulations', 'china', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'sdg9', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('8a03c890-1c10-5289-bc53-37a2316eb2c6', 'China Green Industry Guidance Catalogue (2019 Edition)', 'Green Industry Guidance Catalogue (2019 Edition)', 'The "Green Industry Guidance Catalog (2019 Edition)" provides a comprehensive framework to promote sustainable economic development in China. The catalog delineates green industries into six broad categories: energy saving and environmental protection, cleaner production, clean energy, eco-environmental industries, green infrastructure upgrades, and green services. It emphasizes the development of high-efficiency and energy-saving technologies, pollution control systems, resource recycling, and renewable energy utilization. Key initiatives include the manufacturing of advanced energy-saving equipment, retrofitting industrial systems for efficiency, managing water and soil pollution, and adopting clean energy solutions like solar, wind, and nuclear power. Additionally, the document highlights the importance of green urban planning, ecological restoration, and sustainable agricultural practices. Supporting services such as environmental monitoring, carbon emissions trading, and technical certifications for green products are also covered.

This catalog serves as a guideline for industries and governments to align with China''s broader environmental goals, fostering innovation, reducing carbon emissions, and advancing resource conservation across multiple sectors.', 'The "Green Industry Guidance Catalog (2019 Edition)" provides a comprehensive framework to promote sustainable economic development in China. The catalog delineates green industries into six broad categories: energy saving and environmental protection, cleaner production, clean energy, eco-environmental industries, green infrastructure upgrades, and green services. It emphasizes the development of high-efficiency and energy-saving technologies, pollution control systems, resource recycling, and renewable energy utilization. Key initiatives include the manufacturing of advanced energy-saving equipment, retrofitting industrial systems for efficiency, managing water and soil pollution, and adopting clean energy solutions like solar, wind, and nuclear power. Additionally, the document highlights the importance of green urban planning, ecological restoration, and sustainable agricultural practices. Supporting services such as environmental monitoring, carbon emissions trading, and technical certifications for green products are also covered.

This catalog serves as a guideline for industries and governments to align with China''s broader environmental goals, fostering innovation, reducing carbon emissions, and advancing resource conservation across multiple sectors.', 'The "Green Industry Guidance Catalog (2019 Edition)" provides a comprehensive framework to promote sustainable economic development in China. The catalog delineates green industries into six broad categories: energy saving and environmental protection, cleaner production, clean energy, eco-environmental industries, green infrastructure upgrades, and green services. It emphasizes the development of high-efficiency and energy-saving technologies, pollution control systems, resource recycling, and renewable energy utilization. Key initiatives include the manufacturing of advanced energy-saving equipment, retrofitting industrial systems for efficiency, managing water and soil pollution, and adopting clean energy solutions like solar, wind, and nuclear power. Additionally, the document highlights the importance of green urban planning, ecological restoration, and sustainable agricultural practices. Supporting services such as environmental monitoring, carbon emissions trading, and technical certifications for green products are also covered.

This catalog serves as a guideline for industries and governments to align with China''s broader environmental goals, fostering innovation, reducing carbon emissions, and advancing resource conservation across multiple sectors.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2019-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_25', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'sdg13', 'sdg7', 'china', 'mandatory', 'sdg6', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'sdg15', 'sdg9']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('aa353b87-ac6f-5493-a150-9ffc6294e6d0', 'China Listing of Stocks on the Science and Technology', 'Rules for the Listing of Stocks on the Science and Technology Innovation Board of the Shanghai Stock Exchange', 'The "Rules for the Listing of Stocks on the Science and Technology Innovation Board of the Shanghai Stock Exchange" establishes a regulatory framework to support and guide the development of innovative science and technology enterprises. The policy aims to enhance market fairness, transparency, and investor protection by setting strict requirements for stock listings, information disclosures, and ongoing supervision of listed companies. Key features include:

Detailed criteria for IPOs, including minimum share capital and profitability thresholds.

Standards for continuous disclosure of financial and operational information to ensure transparency.

Mechanisms for risk management, supervision of major transactions, and protection against insider trading and market manipulation.

Provisions for handling delistings, ensuring compliance with financial and operational benchmarks.

Obligations for directors, supervisors, and senior management to maintain corporate governance and fulfill disclosure duties.

The policy emphasizes fostering technological innovation by creating a supportive environment for research-intensive companies while maintaining robust oversight to safeguard market integrity.', 'The "Rules for the Listing of Stocks on the Science and Technology Innovation Board of the Shanghai Stock Exchange" establishes a regulatory framework to support and guide the development of innovative science and technology enterprises. The policy aims to enhance market fairness, transparency, and investor protection by setting strict requirements for stock listings, information disclosures, and ongoing supervision of listed companies. Key features include:

Detailed criteria for IPOs, including minimum share capital and profitability thresholds.

Standards for continuous disclosure of financial and operational information to ensure transparency.

Mechanisms for risk management, supervision of major transactions, and protection against insider trading and market manipulation.

Provisions for handling delistings, ensuring compliance with financial and operational benchmarks.

Obligations for directors, supervisors, and senior management to maintain corporate governance and fulfill disclosure duties.

The policy emphasizes fostering technological innovation by creating a supportive environment for research-intensive companies while maintaining robust oversight to safeguard market integrity.', 'The "Rules for the Listing of Stocks on the Science and Technology Innovation Board of the Shanghai Stock Exchange" establishes a regulatory framework to support and guide the development of innovative science and technology enterprises. The policy aims to enhance market fairness, transparency, and investor protection by setting strict requirements for stock listings, information disclosures, and ongoing supervision of listed companies. Key features include:

Detailed criteria for IPOs, including minimum share capital and profitability thresholds.

Standards for continuous disclosure of financial and operational information to ensure transparency.

Mechanisms for risk management, supervision of major transactions, and protection against insider trading and market manipulation.

Provisions for handling delistings, ensuring compliance with financial and operational benchmarks.

Obligations for directors, supervisors, and senior management to maintain corporate governance and fulfill disclosure duties.

The policy emphasizes fostering technological innovation by creating a supportive environment for research-intensive companies while maintaining robust oversight to safeguard market integrity.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2019-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_31', ARRAY['sdg14', 'regulations', 'china', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'sdg9', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('0b42a767-89c6-523d-90c2-a56e6704fd2b', 'Guiding Opinions of the China Banking and Insurance', 'Guiding Opinions of the China Banking and Insurance Regulatory Commission on Promoting the High-quality Development of the Banking and Insurance Industry', 'These Opinions advocate to adhere to the people-centered development philosophy, implement the new development concept of "innovation, coordination, green, openness, and sharing", deepen the structural reform of the financial supply side, expand the opening of the financial industry, and improve the highly adaptable, competitive, and inclusive modern financial system, continuously improve the quality and efficiency of financial services to the real economy, and effectively prevent and resolve financial risks.', 'These Opinions advocate to adhere to the people-centered development philosophy, implement the new development concept of "innovation, coordination, green, openness, and sharing", deepen the structural reform of the financial supply side, expand the opening of the financial industry, and improve the highly adaptable, competitive, and inclusive modern financial system, continuously improve the quality and efficiency of financial services to the real economy, and effectively prevent and resolve financial risks.', 'These Opinions advocate to adhere to the people-centered development philosophy, implement the new development concept of "innovation, coordination, green, openness, and sharing", deepen the structural reform of the financial supply side, expand the opening of the financial industry, and improve the highly adaptable, competitive, and inclusive modern financial system, continuously improve the quality and efficiency of financial services to the real economy, and effectively prevent and resolve financial risks.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2019-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_60', ARRAY['sdg9', 'mandatory', 'mandatory_regulations', 'disclosure', 'china', 'sdg3']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('2dddcb97-cbcc-5ca6-87e5-f4f90ce1970a', 'China Social Responsibility Guidelines for Chinese Industrial Enterprises', 'Social Responsibility Guidelines for Chinese Industrial Enterprises and Industrial Associations (Second Edition)', 'These guidelines strive to not only reflect the basic concepts and requirements of social responsibility, but also reflect the current situation and characteristics of industrial enterprises and industrial associations in fulfilling social responsibility; it not only has the function of publicizing and implementing social responsibility awareness, but also meets the actual needs of social responsibility management of industrial enterprises and industrial associations; both It conforms to the development trend of international corporate social responsibility and leads the practice direction of Chinese corporate social responsibility. This edition of the "Guide" clarifies the common understanding of Chinese industrial enterprises and industrial associations in the field of social responsibility, including the basic principles, general requirements, social responsibility system, main content of social responsibility, and reference for the preparation of social responsibility reports. This edition of the Guidelines is applicable to Chinese industrial enterprises and industrial associations to build social responsibility systems, promote social responsibility management, and disclose social responsibility information to continuously improve social responsibility performance.', 'These guidelines strive to not only reflect the basic concepts and requirements of social responsibility, but also reflect the current situation and characteristics of industrial enterprises and industrial associations in fulfilling social responsibility; it not only has the function of publicizing and implementing social responsibility awareness, but also meets the actual needs of social responsibility management of industrial enterprises and industrial associations; both It conforms to the development trend of international corporate social responsibility and leads the practice direction of Chinese corporate social responsibility. This edition of the "Guide" clarifies the common understanding of Chinese industrial enterprises and industrial associations in the field of social responsibility, including the basic principles, general requirements, social responsibility system, main content of social responsibility, and reference for the preparation of social responsibility reports. This edition of the Guidelines is applicable to Chinese industrial enterprises and industrial associations to build social responsibility systems, promote social responsibility management, and disclose social responsibility information to continuously improve social responsibility performance.', 'These guidelines strive to not only reflect the basic concepts and requirements of social responsibility, but also reflect the current situation and characteristics of industrial enterprises and industrial associations in fulfilling social responsibility; it not only has the function of publicizing and implementing social responsibility awareness, but also meets the actual needs of social responsibility management of industrial enterprises and industrial associations; both It conforms to the development trend of international corporate social responsibility and leads the practice direction of Chinese corporate social responsibility. This edition of the "Guide" clarifies the common understanding of Chinese industrial enterprises and industrial associations in the field of social responsibility, including the basic principles, general requirements, social responsibility system, main content of social responsibility, and reference for the preparation of social responsibility reports. This edition of the Guidelines is applicable to Chinese industrial enterprises and industrial associations to build social responsibility systems, promote social responsibility management, and disclose social responsibility information to continuously improve social responsibility performance.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2019-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_61', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'sdg9', 'sdg7', 'disclosure', 'china', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('4faaa2a4-2d67-595c-b3ba-692f4fa5e17c', 'China Social Responsibility in Outbound Mining Investments (GSRM)', 'Guidelines for Social Responsibility in Outbound Mining Investments (GSRM)', 'The Guidelines lay out of a series of principles for companies conducting activities relating to mining internationally, in accordance with CSR principles.These principles largely span corporate social responsibility, namely : human rights, labour rights, environment, stakeholders'' implication, responsible value chains, transparency.', 'The Guidelines lay out of a series of principles for companies conducting activities relating to mining internationally, in accordance with CSR principles.These principles largely span corporate social responsibility, namely : human rights, labour rights, environment, stakeholders'' implication, responsible value chains, transparency.', 'The Guidelines lay out of a series of principles for companies conducting activities relating to mining internationally, in accordance with CSR principles.These principles largely span corporate social responsibility, namely : human rights, labour rights, environment, stakeholders'' implication, responsible value chains, transparency.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2018-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_1', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'sdg8', 'sdg7', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'china', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('a31db9bd-bbfd-57eb-9ed4-c98f13ff6061', 'China Green Investment Guidelines (For Trial Implementation)', 'Green Investment Guidelines (For Trial Implementation)', 'These guidelines set out to practice the requirements laid out by the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with regard to developing green finance and promoting a sound economic system that facilitates green, low-carbon, and circular development, implementing the Guidelines for Establishing the Green Financial System.', 'These guidelines set out to practice the requirements laid out by the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with regard to developing green finance and promoting a sound economic system that facilitates green, low-carbon, and circular development, implementing the Guidelines for Establishing the Green Financial System.', 'These guidelines set out to practice the requirements laid out by the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with regard to developing green finance and promoting a sound economic system that facilitates green, low-carbon, and circular development, implementing the Guidelines for Establishing the Green Financial System.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2018-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_26', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'sdg13', 'sdg7', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'china', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('0d96b3f2-3cbf-5eec-88ef-5cd247b994da', 'China Shanghai Stock Exchange Serves Green Development and Promotes', 'Shanghai Stock Exchange Serves Green Development and Promotes Green Finance Vision and Action Plan (2018-2020)', 'A plan for giving full play to the function of the capital market to optimize resource allocation, serve China’s economic transformation, optimize economic structure, transform growth drivers, cultivate new economic growth points, and promote high-quality development. It also seeks to accelerate the establishment of relevant standards for green finance in the capital market, steadily innovate and develop relevant green financial products, gradually cultivate and expand the group of green investors, expand direct financing channels for green industries, strengthen international cooperation in the field of green finance in the capital market, and jointly promote green development and sustainability.', 'A plan for giving full play to the function of the capital market to optimize resource allocation, serve China’s economic transformation, optimize economic structure, transform growth drivers, cultivate new economic growth points, and promote high-quality development. It also seeks to accelerate the establishment of relevant standards for green finance in the capital market, steadily innovate and develop relevant green financial products, gradually cultivate and expand the group of green investors, expand direct financing channels for green industries, strengthen international cooperation in the field of green finance in the capital market, and jointly promote green development and sustainability.', 'A plan for giving full play to the function of the capital market to optimize resource allocation, serve China’s economic transformation, optimize economic structure, transform growth drivers, cultivate new economic growth points, and promote high-quality development. It also seeks to accelerate the establishment of relevant standards for green finance in the capital market, steadily innovate and develop relevant green financial products, gradually cultivate and expand the group of green investors, expand direct financing channels for green industries, strengthen international cooperation in the field of green finance in the capital market, and jointly promote green development and sustainability.', 'China', 'climate', 'in_force', '2018-01-01'::date, 'China', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/33_33', ARRAY['regulations', 'sdg7', 'sdg17', 'mandatory', 'disclosure', 'china']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('a2c190ab-c7fe-50f2-beef-b37cf2b839e2', 'China CSRC Announcement (2018) (证监会公告〔2018〕29号)', 'CSRC Announcement No. 29 (2018) (证监会公告〔2018〕29号)', 'CSRC Announcement No. 29 (2018) is a regulatory directive issued by the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) in 2018. It primarily focuses on enhancing corporate disclosure requirements, particularly in areas such as financial reporting, corporate governance, and sustainability practices. The regulation applies to publicly listed companies in China and aims to align China''s capital markets with international best practices.

Key aspects of the announcement include:

Corporate Governance Standards:
Strengthens board responsibilities in financial oversight.
Mandates internal controls to prevent financial misreporting and fraud.
Financial Disclosure Requirements:
Companies must provide detailed and standardized financial statements.
Disclosure of related-party transactions and risk management strategies.
Sustainability & ESG Reporting:
Encourages voluntary disclosure of environmental, social, and governance (ESG) factors.
Promotes transparency in sustainability-related investments.
Market Supervision & Penalties:
Introduces stricter penalties for false disclosures and non-compliance.
Strengthens CSRC oversight on listed companies'' reporting practices.', 'CSRC Announcement No. 29 (2018) is a regulatory directive issued by the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) in 2018. It primarily focuses on enhancing corporate disclosure requirements, particularly in areas such as financial reporting, corporate governance, and sustainability practices. The regulation applies to publicly listed companies in China and aims to align China''s capital markets with international best practices.

Key aspects of the announcement include:

Corporate Governance Standards:
Strengthens board responsibilities in financial oversight.
Mandates internal controls to prevent financial misreporting and fraud.
Financial Disclosure Requirements:
